NAME
    ping - send ICMP echo requests (network test)

SYNOPSIS
    ping TARGET [COUNT]

DESCRIPTION
    Sends an IPv4 ICMP echo request to TARGET and reports the
    round-trip time the kernel measured. Used to check that the NIC is
    up: on QEMU's default user network the host router answers at
    10.0.2.2, so 'ping 10.0.2.2' is a quick connectivity smoke test.

    TARGET is a dotted-quad address or a host name. Names are resolved
    through /etc/hosts first, then via DNS: A queries to each
    'nameserver' line of /etc/resolv.conf (default server 1.1.1.1),
    tried in order. COUNT (default 4) picks how many requests to send
    before printing a summary; each request waits at most 300 ms in the
    kernel (ARP resolution for a new target, via the gateway off
    subnet).

FILES
    /etc/hosts
    /etc/resolv.conf

EXIT STATUS
    0 if at least one reply arrived, 1 otherwise; 2 on bad usage or an
    unknown host.

EXAMPLES
    ping 10.0.2.2
    ping gateway 1
    ping 10.0.2.2 1
